Subject: [PATCH 08101/11362] Where the live agent's actions actually come
 from: 3,600 actions accounted for, one branch at a time

The mediation null was an inference from three indirect lines (LLM-tier deletion left 5 of
6 games byte-identical; 0/22 stall inductions cleared the goal gate; tn36 held a held-out
accuracy 1.0 engine and banked nothing). None of them measured the ACTION. This does.

Nine observed episodes of the SCORED E3AgentPolicy on the OFFLINE arcade, 5 games x 3
replicates, live gemma-4-31B-it-qat induction on GPU 1, 3,600 actions each attributed to
the branch that chose it.

  * FAILED episodes: 123 of 2,400 actions (5.1%) were plan-derived. Per-episode median 0.0.
  * BANKED episodes: 7 of 1,200 (0.58%) -- the episodes that bank plan LESS, not more.
  * Of 5 level-ups, 4 were emitted by explore.explorer and ALL FOUR happened strictly
    before the pipeline had emitted its first action, so it cannot have caused them.
  * The 5th is the pipeline's one clean win: lp85 induced a 12-step plan whose 5th step
    banked a level. The honest answer is not "the pipeline never works".

Where it is lost partitions cleanly, one mode per game: tr87/ft09 induce an engine whose
held-out accuracy is 0.0 and it is never trusted; lp85 trusts the engine (1.0) but the goal
predicate is degenerate so no plan exists; tn36 has a perfect engine, a satisfiable goal,
finds a 61-step plan, executes it to completion with every step changing the frame -- and
reaches no level.

The obvious objection is answered in the data, not in prose: 0 of 9 episodes hit the
induction cap, so the cap never bound and the low share is the agent's own stall detector
declining to re-engage, including after a plan has already failed.

Two controls worth more than they cost. The wall-truncation rule was pre-registered before
the first cell landed and it cuts AGAINST the headline -- it excludes a vc33 episode that
banked a level with zero plan-derived actions; adding all 5 excluded episodes back moves
the failed share 5.125% -> 4.897%. And the A/A control produced an unlooked-for result: on
vc33 and tr87 two same-seed replicates, each with an INDEPENDENTLY SAMPLED 31B induction,
produced byte-identical 400-action sequences -- an independent reproduction of the
LLM-tier-inert finding, from a different direction, on the scored policy.

Also commits python/carnot/agentic/arc_action_provenance.py, which was UNTRACKED while
HEAD's arc_competition_agent.py already carried an unguarded import of it inside
E3AgentPolicy.__init__ (line ~4465). A fresh clone of HEAD could not construct the scored
agent at all. The probe/worker are committed for the same reason: the census driver spawns
them.

adversarial_verify: 0 flagged. 37 tests pass.

